<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Coscinodiscus wailesii Turing wavelength at 4.3 mm (Holocene, chronoseries 1/1) — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring maps each symbol onto Turing 1952 and Schnakenberg 1979, and the Lean namespace MathOfBiology.Loop_3156 restates the integer band conditions. The spatial step is explicitly a transfer of a well-mixed paper." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Coscinodiscus wailesii Turing wavelength at 4.3 mm (Holocene, chronoseries 1/1) — Model fidelity to source: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The PDE, Jacobian, and sigma_+ maximizer are implemented (sigma_plus, sigma_max_wavenumber). The det-minimizer is kept only as a negative control and anti-correlates with the spectrum. Pass 1 still headlines the power-spectrum peak, which is systematically longer than sigma_+ (RMSE 1.453 length units), so the reported comparison is not yet the linear growth rate." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Coscinodiscus wailesii Turing wavelength at 4.3 mm (Holocene, chronoseries 1/1) — Morphometric validation: 76/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Power-spectrum Pearson r = 0.9899 against lambda_sigma, with RMSE = 1.453 length units. Upper-left areola pitch is 10.15 px (CV 0.268, n = 718) against simulated pitch 14.06 px (CV 0.086). KS distance on median-normalised diameters is 0.317. The RMSE is a real bias, so this pass does not treat the fit as closed." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
